# R6 blast-radius denylist — the FRAMEWORK DEFAULT, machine-readable half of
# references/blast-radius-denylist.md.
#
# This list is used only when the target repo's conventions file
# (`stack.conventions_file`, default .claude/loops/conventions.json) has an EMPTY
# `blast_radius_denylist_globs`. When that array is non-empty it REPLACES this file —
# the adopter owns the list — so an adopter who writes their own must cover the same
# five categories (migrations, secrets, auth, infra/IaC, CI) in their own stack's names.
#
# One glob per line; '#' comments. Matched case-insensitively (fnmatch) against the
# repo-relative path; a pattern starting with '*/' also matches at the repo root; a
# pattern without a '/' also matches the basename. A hit BLOCKS: dev-fix returns
# status "blocked-blast-radius", ship preflight aborts. Err toward blocking: a hit
# forces a human gate, it does not delete work. Content-level rules (an auth section
# inside an otherwise-benign file, a connection string, an authorization
# attribute/decorator) remain the protocol's job — this file is the mechanical floor,
# not the ceiling.

# DB migrations / schema (ORM migrations, schema snapshots, raw DDL)
*/migrations/*
*/migrate/*
*/alembic/*
*schema*snapshot*
schema.rb
structure.sql
*.prisma
*.sql

# Secrets / env config
.env*
*.env
*.env.*
*secrets*
*secret.*
*credentials*
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.jks

# Auth / authorization wiring
*authorization*polic*
*authentication*config*
*auth*polic*
*auth*config*
*/identity/*
*permissions*.polic*

# Infra / IaC
*.tf
*.tfvars
*.bicep
*/cloudformation/*
Pulumi.*
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
compose.y*ml
*/k8s/*
*/kubernetes/*
*/helm/*
*/charts/*
*/terraform/*
*/infra/*
*/iac/*

# CI / pipeline definitions
.github/workflows/*
.gitlab-ci*
Jenkinsfile*
.circleci/*
.buildkite/*
.drone.y*ml
*pipelines*.yml
*pipelines*.yaml
*/pipelines/*
